{"items":[{"id":"EUVD-2026-124536","enisaUuid":"5d66c2f8-6998-3679-96a2-1eb266a9c86b","description":"A flaw was found in freeradius. An improper length validation in the EAP-FAST module allows a stack-based buffer overflow during session ticket processing. A remote, unauthenticated attacker can exploit this flaw by sending a specially crafted handshake request, causing the server process to crash and resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS).","datePublished":"Nov 12, 2026, 4:21:52 PM","dateUpdated":"Nov 23, 2026, 2:57:22 PM","baseScore":7.5,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","references":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-127030\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d2572340\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/064567a08f3b9d9b4863fab6060fafe296ac7de9\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/a5d09dad528d7a3a3c4c01158716ab85a12e09ef\n","aliases":"GHSA-6gv4-m6gx-m32r\nCVE-2026-127030\n","assigner":"redhat","epss":0.83,"enisaIdProduct":[],"enisaIdVendor":[]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-124535","enisaUuid":"75f4d8f4-f06a-37db-86a0-05ff3a2fc1b7","description":"A flaw was found in freeradius\u0027s Extensible Authentication Protocol Method for Subscriber Identity Module (EAP-SIM) module. When handling authentication requests, the server copies a client-supplied identity into an internal structure without properly checking its length against a fixed-size buffer. An unauthenticated remote attacker can exploit this issue by sending specially crafted EAP-SIM messages, triggering a stack buffer overflow that crashes the service and results in a Denial of Service (DoS).","datePublished":"Nov 12, 2026, 4:21:48 PM","dateUpdated":"Nov 23, 2026, 2:57:21 PM","baseScore":7.5,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","references":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-127029\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id\u003d2572339\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/064567a08f3b9d9b4863fab6060fafe296ac7de9\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/e415f818dcdf91626e5e7314b3a4f819ab11f572\n","aliases":"GHSA-gfm6-4qp3-m8ch\nCVE-2026-127029\n","assigner":"redhat","epss":1.0,"enisaIdProduct":[],"enisaIdVendor":[]},{"id":"EUVD-2026-95808","enisaUuid":"a25e5445-078d-3ad7-a203-626e14f41d12","description":"PHPNuxBill through 2025.3.20 contains an unauthenticated SQL injection vulnerability in the radius.php FreeRADIUS REST endpoint that interpolates request parameters into whereRaw() queries. Attackers can send crafted username, macAddr or nasid parameters to the accounting or authenticate actions to extract customer records and credentials via time-based blind SQL injection.","datePublished":"Oct 9, 2026, 2:33:30 PM","dateUpdated":"Oct 9, 2026, 2:46:56 PM","baseScore":9.3,"baseScoreVersion":"4.0","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","references":"https://github.com/hotspotbilling/phpnuxbill/security/advisories/GHSA-q8ch-r8cv-q579\nhttps://github.com/hotspotbilling/phpnuxbill/blob/2025.3.13/radius.php#L277\nhttps://github.com/hotspotbilling/phpnuxbill\nhttps://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpnuxbill-through-2025.3.20-unauthenticated-sql-injection-via-radius-php\n","aliases":"CVE-2026-108107\nGHSA-8g3m-4qjp-58m6\n","assigner":"VulnCheck","epss":0.56,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"ddc41207-adda-3fd6-8c02-6652f8845c2b","product":{"name":"phpnuxbill","vendor":{"name":"hotspotbilling"}},"product_version":"0 ≤2025.3.20"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"dc7ff7ad-b283-3127-83a1-fb6692497c45","vendor":{"name":"hotspotbilling"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2022-45025","enisaUuid":"ee41975b-548c-3706-a868-e5895aa30171","description":"A flaw was found in freeradius. A malicious RADIUS client or home server can send a malformed abinary attribute which can cause the server to crash.","datePublished":"Jan 17, 2023, 12:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Nov 3, 2025, 7:27:40 PM","baseScore":6.5,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","references":"https://freeradius.org/security/\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/0ec2b39d260e\n","aliases":"GHSA-3886-rc87-ccgx\nCVE-2022-41861\n","assigner":"redhat","epss":1.31,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"5a192de4-4a56-3af3-8f50-69d45ea7fb93","product":{"name":"freeradius","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"All versions from 0.0.1 to 3.0.25"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"a75d64b5-270e-3d33-9167-b90448b72293","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2022-45024","enisaUuid":"3ec9aa3e-0c50-3cf7-a9c7-8e336f01652a","description":"In freeradius, when an EAP-SIM supplicant sends an unknown SIM option, the server will try to look that option up in the internal dictionaries. This lookup will fail, but the SIM code will not check for that failure. Instead, it will dereference a NULL pointer, and cause the server to crash.","datePublished":"Jan 17, 2023, 12:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Nov 3, 2025, 7:27:38 PM","baseScore":7.5,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","references":"https://freeradius.org/security/\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/f1cdbb33ec61c4a64a\n","aliases":"CVE-2022-41860\nGHSA-cfm7-f9p7-7m2w\n","assigner":"redhat","epss":1.42,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"273b0ce9-40e2-3753-b90a-81c850727434","product":{"name":"freeradius","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"All versions from 0.9.3 to 3.0.25"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"2539df1a-2028-3d93-bc19-5b0020de4500","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2022-45023","enisaUuid":"af7ef963-eb44-3843-9dbb-7392eebd2f89","description":"In freeradius, the EAP-PWD function compute_password_element() leaks information about the password which allows an attacker to substantially reduce the size of an offline dictionary attack.","datePublished":"Jan 17, 2023, 12:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Nov 3, 2025, 7:27:37 PM","baseScore":7.5,"baseScoreVersion":"3.1","baseScoreVector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N","references":"https://freeradius.org/security/\nhttps://github.com/FreeRADIUS/freeradius-server/commit/9e5e8f2f\n","aliases":"CVE-2022-41859\nGHSA-cmvm-c7qf-pmc5\n","assigner":"redhat","epss":1.0,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"b2e4ae55-b1f0-3a07-a8ef-9a195e843ad8","product":{"name":"freeradius","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"unknown"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"acf5c3db-cd19-33e5-ad11-76b3d886db8d","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2002-0315","enisaUuid":"299aa667-7701-3b3a-ae1d-59c924da5051","description":"FreeRADIUS RADIUS server allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption) via a flood of Access-Request packets.","datePublished":"Apr 2, 2003, 5:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Aug 8, 2024, 2:42:29 AM","baseScore":null,"references":"http://marc.info/?l\u003dbugtraq\u0026m\u003d101440113410083\u0026w\u003d2\nhttp://www.iss.net/security_center/static/9968.php\n","aliases":"CVE-2002-0318\nGHSA-56mp-3v3v-cq2j\n","assigner":"mitre","epss":1.45,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"bfa1a511-1075-3ebd-bc83-174c436d9402","product":{"name":"n/a","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"n/a"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"9588247e-b854-3af2-b4e9-78cf0f1fef09","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2003-0958","enisaUuid":"936f2c11-dccd-3338-8978-daa592ce8014","description":"Stack-based buffer overflow in SMB_Logon_Server of the rlm_smb experimental module for FreeRADIUS 0.9.3 and earlier allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via a long User-Password attribute.","datePublished":"Dec 2, 2003, 5:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Aug 8, 2024, 2:12:35 AM","baseScore":null,"references":"http://marc.info/?l\u003dbugtraq\u0026m\u003d106986437621130\u0026w\u003d2\n","aliases":"CVE-2003-0968\nGHSA-cq56-hhrj-4j8p\n","assigner":"mitre","epss":3.96,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"344d803c-621c-3a72-8f46-bbff25bde3b8","product":{"name":"n/a","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"n/a"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"90f2e1a2-de67-3c14-8c8d-ab051ee2418d","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2003-0957","enisaUuid":"6af4a585-d310-3e56-993a-cb7456b93c6d","description":"rad_decode in FreeRADIUS 0.9.2 and earlier allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) via a short RADIUS string attribute with a tag, which causes memcpy to be called with a -1 length argument, as demonstrated using the Tunnel-Password attribute.","datePublished":"Dec 2, 2003, 5:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Aug 8, 2024, 2:12:34 AM","baseScore":null,"references":"http://marc.info/?l\u003dbugtraq\u0026m\u003d106935911101493\u0026w\u003d2\nhttp://marc.info/?l\u003dfreeradius-users\u0026m\u003d106947389449613\u0026w\u003d2\nhttp://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2003-386.html\nhttps://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A10917\nhttp://marc.info/?l\u003dbugtraq\u0026m\u003d106944220426970\n","aliases":"GHSA-4j6g-2g2g-f47h\nCVE-2003-0967\n","assigner":"mitre","epss":4.76,"enisaIdProduct":[{"id":"804edebd-10b8-3649-b9c8-04d4e21a65bb","product":{"name":"n/a","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}},"product_version":"n/a"}],"enisaIdVendor":[{"id":"dea9f6f2-f2dd-31ea-adee-6a1e3eaaabe6","vendor":{"name":"n/a"}}]},{"id":"EUVD-2004-0959","enisaUuid":"f8646027-0786-3b35-8775-0e867d93fb85","description":"Memory leak in FreeRADIUS before 1.0.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (memory exhaustion) via a series of Access-Request packets with (1) Ascend-Send-Secret, (2) Ascend-Recv-Secret, or (3) Tunnel-Password attributes.","datePublished":"Oct 20, 2004, 4:00:00 AM","dateUpdated":"Aug 8, 2024, 12:31:48 AM","baseScore":null,"references":"http://security.gentoo.org/glsa/glsa-200409-29.xml\nhttps://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A10024\nhttp://www.securityfocus.com/bid/11222\nhttps://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/17440\nhttp://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/541574\n","aliases":"CVE-2004-0